tttypes: install the .ptype sources alongside types.xdr

programs/tttypes compiles nine .ptype files into types.xdr at build time
and installs only that:

    BUILT_SOURCES = types.xdr
    dist_tttypes_DATA = $(BUILT_SOURCES)

That is sufficient for ToolTalk itself -- _Tt_typedb::tt_path() has
$(CDE_INSTALLATION_TOP)/appconfig/tttypes/types.xdr on its default search
list (lib/tt/slib/mp_typedb.C), so the compiled database is found and read
whenever TTPATH is unset.

substrate also wants the sources present on the target, so the ptypes can
be re-merged into a user or session type database at runtime with
`tt_type_comp -m`.  /etc/rc.d/16-ttdbserver does exactly that: it globs
*.ptype in the installed tttypes directory and compiles each one.  With
only types.xdr installed, that glob is empty, the loop is gated off by
its own `[ -n "$ptypes" ]` test, and the script silently does nothing
beyond starting rpc.ttdbserver.

Add the .ptype files to the installed set.  The list is derived from
LOCALDEPFILES rather than written out again, so it cannot drift from the
set the build actually compiles.

diff --git a/programs/tttypes/Makefile.am b/programs/tttypes/Makefile.am
index 47471a49..af0bd996 100644
--- a/programs/tttypes/Makefile.am
+++ b/programs/tttypes/Makefile.am
@@ -23,7 +23,19 @@ BUILT_SOURCES = types.xdr
 CLEANFILES = *.done types.xdr .tt_lock
 
 tttypesdir = $(CDE_INSTALLATION_TOP)/appconfig/tttypes
-dist_tttypes_DATA = $(BUILT_SOURCES)
+
+# Install the .ptype sources alongside the compiled types.xdr.  Upstream
+# ships only types.xdr, which is enough for ToolTalk itself -- tt_path()
+# has $(CDE_INSTALLATION_TOP)/appconfig/tttypes/types.xdr on its default
+# search list.  substrate additionally wants the sources on the target so
+# that the ptypes can be re-merged into a user or session type database
+# at runtime with `tt_type_comp -m`, which is what /etc/rc.d/16-ttdbserver
+# does; it globs *.ptype in this directory and silently does nothing when
+# only types.xdr is installed.
+#
+# Derived from LOCALDEPFILES so the list cannot drift from the set the
+# build actually compiles.
+dist_tttypes_DATA = $(BUILT_SOURCES) $(LOCALDEPFILES:.done=.ptype)
 
 types.xdr: $(LOCALDEPFILES)
 
